all right my talk at the table is about  schools reopening this fall with daily  coronavirus cases increasing in dozens  of states  teachers all across the country are  voicing concern about the health risks  while most teachers agree that  face-to-face learning is better for  students many also wonder at what cost  a study by the kaiser kaiser family  foundation found that about one in four  teachers one in four  have a condition that puts them at a  higher risk of serious illness  from the virus so what we did is we  asked a diverse group of teachers from  four states  about how they feel going back c-a-p  my name is carla reyes i am a special  education teacher  i am a middle school science teacher at  a small private school in minneapolis  minnesota  my name is dr kai rush and i am a high  school teacher  in clearwater florida  i am an esl teacher in dallas texas  i definitely want to get us back into  school safely there are kids who are in  unsafe places  and school is their safe place to be  i want to see my students smiling faces  in front of the classroom  but do i want students to come back i  want them to come back  safely not all schools have soap  not all schools have potable water  there's a lot to consider when you're  reopening  school buildings where hundreds of  people are coming into contact with each  other every day  i feel very uneasy returning to  face-to-face instruction  because i am putting my children at  risk of contracting covert 19.  going back to school is not going to  mean  going back to school the way we remember  it being  we are going to have reduced class sizes  we are going to have distancing the less  they get close to each other the better  everything is going to be different and  that is  okay let's talk about this the federal  government and city governments need to  step  up and invest in education and all the  different guarantees to make sure  that we don't die i have underlying  conditions  and i like to support my students but if  i  pass from this disease i won't be able  to  support my students or my young adult  children we did not get into this  profession for the money  we got into this profession because we  love kids  and while you're not there we're there  and we want to make sure that they have  the best environment possible  before going back  [Music]  you
 

